<dict>
	<key>content</key>
	<string>Act as an expert ${1:programmer,historian,philosopher,capital allocator}. Your objective is to [briefly state the primary goal].

&lt;context&gt;
[Provide the necessary background. Treat this as the raw data and hypotheses the model needs to understand the operating environment. E.g., "We are analyzing opportunity costs for a capital allocation decision..."]
&lt;/context&gt;

&lt;task&gt;
[State exactly what needs to be done. E.g., "Analyze the provided dataset, identify the three largest cost-utility mismatches, and propose alternative capital allocations."]
&lt;/task&gt;

&lt;rules&gt;
- [Constraint 1: e.g., "Do not use qualitative generalizations; rely strictly on quantitative metrics."]
- [Constraint 2: e.g., "If assumptions must be made to bridge data gaps, explicitly surface them."]
- [Constraint 3: e.g., "Exclude any analysis of sunk costs."]
&lt;/rules&gt;

&lt;output_format&gt;
Provide the final output strictly in the following format:
1. Executive Summary (max 3 sentences)
2. Markdown Table detailing the top 3 mismatches (Columns: Asset, Stated Utility, Actual Cost, Opportunity Cost)
3. Proposed Alternatives (Bullet points)
&lt;/output_format&gt;

&lt;input_data&gt;
[Insert any raw text, data, code, or variables here]
&lt;/input_data&gt;</string>
